      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p>TEST DETAILS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>Marker Tested : PCNA (Proliferating Cell Nuclear Antigen)<br>Clone &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; : __________________________<br>Control &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; : Positive Control Used<br>Method &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;: Immunohistochemistry</p>\n<p>RESULTS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>Marker : PCNA<br>Result : Positive / Negative / Focal<br>Staining Pattern : Nuclear staining<br>Proliferation Index (%) : ________</p>\n<p>INTERPRETATION CRITERIA<br>-----------------------------------------<br>- PCNA Positive: Nuclear staining in tumor cells indicates active proliferation<br>- PCNA Negative: No significant proliferative activity detected<br>- Proliferation Index:<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Low &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;: &lt;30%<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Moderate : 30&ndash;70%<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; High &nbsp; &nbsp; : &gt;70%</p>\n<p>IMPRESSION<br>-----------------------------------------<br>[ ] PCNA Positive &ndash; Suggests high proliferative activity<br>[ ] PCNA Negative &ndash; Low or absent proliferative activity<br>[ ] Correlate with Ki-67 for more accurate proliferation assessment</p>\n<p>COMMENTS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>- PCNA is a marker of cell proliferation but less specific than Ki-67.<br>- Use in conjunction with other markers and histopathological findings for tumor grading.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
